Bundled Spanish vocabulary selection credits wordfreq by Robyn Speer (data
CC BY-SA 4.0) for frequency ordering; see docs/UPSTREAM-CURRICULUM-MISSION.md.
The coarse frequency bands in extension/src/vocabulary.js and the rounded
frequency table in data/curriculum/es/wordfreq-bands.csv were derived from
wordfreq 3.1.1 by Robyn Speer (https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq). Its
underlying data is CC BY-SA 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The table rounds Zipf
values to two decimals and maps their lower Spanish/English score to a band;
the Beginner 30 are assigned band 0 by product rule. The table is distributed
under CC BY-SA 4.0. The licence and native-review ruling for future new
vocabulary rows remains open.

The scheduler in extension/src/fsrs.js is an independent port of the published
FSRS-6 algorithm (Free Spaced Repetition Scheduler, open-spaced-repetition,
https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition). Its default parameter values are
the FSRS-6 defaults published with py-fsrs and ts-fsrs, which are MIT licensed
(Copyright (c) open-spaced-repetition contributors). No upstream source code is
vendored.
